  "premise_review": [
    "Both theorems retain every exact original implicit C/F/nabla/e/X and explicit T : Folder.CrystallineTensor.FixedTensor nabla e X hypothesis. All fully qualified source types and both fully qualified forwarding proof calls are copied unchanged.",
    "The horizontal conclusion is the application of the predicate supplied by the original connection to exactly T.tensor.underlyingSection. The other conclusion is the actual equation e.map X T.tensor.underlyingSection = T.tensor.underlyingSection, not an arbitrary independently selected named fixedness proposition.",
    "The full original FixedTensor provider was independently read as primary187. Its coherent complete record requires exactly the TensorSection, horizontal proof and actual map equality supplied by T; no new record, local independent bare Prop or field-dropping extraction is substituted.",
    "The exact Connection body selects horizontal as an arbitrary predicate without defining it as a differential kernel. CrystalEndomorphism is only a family of pointwise section maps. Neither theorem imposes heat compatibility, constructs a tensor algebra, proves analytic flatness or adds missing restriction/naturality laws.",
    "Both are genuine conditional forwarding proofs. The source constructs no T, fixed section, existence witness or uniqueness result, and the statements preserve all supplied premises even when not used separately by the forwarded projection.",
    "Keep the two closely related projection consequences together as one coherent component: they concern the same supplied T and exact same underlyingSection. No historical provider is replaced by newly reviewed GRWTSK source187; the sole original Folder.CrystallineTensor.FixedTensor import and its unresolved historical identity remain unchanged.",
    "Only the containing namespace is rebound; no alias, new legacy self-provider import, body/type edit, kernel replay or mathematical admission is asserted."
  ],
